    "background_story": "Navy was a child prodigy with an extraordinary gift for memorization. By the age of 5, she could recite the entire alphabet backwards and forwards, and by 10, she had memorized the entire script of her favorite musical. As she grew older, Navy's talent only intensified, and she began to compete in national memory championships. She could recall entire books, phone numbers, and even the order of a deck of cards with ease. Navy's remarkable ability earned her a spot on a popular game show, where she stunned audiences with her ability to recall complex patterns and sequences. She used her gift to help others, creating memory aids for students and even assisting in forensic investigations. Navy's exceptional memory made her a valuable asset in various fields, and she continued to push the boundaries of human memorization.",
